WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
Everyone's obsessing over chat GPT and

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:08.080
almost nobody is using Gemini and

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.960
notebook LM to build a real edge. That's

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.880
a huge mistake. After 20 years as a CEO

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.920
and board member helping build

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.000
billion-dollar companies, one thing is

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:20.520
clear to me. The edge is never the tool.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.040
It's the system you build. That's why

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.720
mastering Google's AI tools like Gemini

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.760
and notebook LM matters a lot. In this

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:30.760
video, I'll show you how to build a

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.560
four-part human intelligence system so

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.560
effectively [music] it almost feels

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:38.040
unfair. So you can learn faster, think

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:41.360
clearer, and build an advantage that

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.360
puts you ahead of 99% of the people in

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.280
the room. So let's get started. But

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.960
before we get to the system, we need to

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:51.720
understand a framework that separates

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:54.200
the top 1% in how they use AI. An MIT

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:57.360
Media Lab study found that people

00:00:54.200 --> 00:01:00.320
relying on AI for writing showed the

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:03.360
weakest brain connectivity and recall.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:07.040
This is machine fog. When it comes to

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:10.200
AI, most people are building on sand. No

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.440
blueprint, no foundation, no floors.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.760
What you need instead is a strong

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:17.840
intelligence architecture that's built

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:20.400
on a bedrock. Four floors, four

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:24.080
different jobs. The ground floor is your

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:26.320
grounding. AI has a dangerous habit. It

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:29.320
can sound convincing without being

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:32.240
accurate. It's like a brilliant lawyer

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:34.760
who argues beautifully while fabricating

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:37.800
the evidence. This is where Google's

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:40.520
notebook LM comes handy because it works

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:44.000
only from the material you give it. Your

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:46.600
documents, your notes, your transcripts,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.480
your data. Notebook LM does not give you

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:51.640
just a response. It gives you the

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:54.080
receipt. You can upload a 500-page

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:56.880
textbook, the last 6 months of your

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.640
meeting transcripts, or that entire pile

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.760
of PDFs waiting on your desktop. It will

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:04.360
take all of it. And then [music] you can

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.720
investigate, ask questions, find

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:10.039
patterns. Instead of artificial

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:12.800
incompetence, you are now anchored in

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:15.200
reality. The next floor is your frontier

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.360
model, Gemini in this case. This is

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:19.840
where you move from evidence to

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:22.560
exploration. You know, Gemini can hold

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:25.440
an enormous amount of data and context

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:28.360
as well. You can feed in 2 million

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:31.040
tokens to its active memory all at once.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:34.240
That's nearly the entire Harry Potter

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:37.040
series plus the entire Lord of the Rings

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:39.200
trilogy, and there's some space left. So

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.360
you can feed it a decade of your

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.920
company's financial history and

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.640
thousands of customer call transcripts,

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:49.200
and it will still identify the hidden

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.280
patterns a human eye would take months

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.000
to spot. It doesn't just find that

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:56.120
needle in the haystack, it understands

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.640
the entire harvesting season. Now, the

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:00.920
next floor is your specialist. You know,

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.280
when you start with AI, it always feels

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:05.560
like you're talking to a complete random

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.040
stranger you just met at a train

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:10.400
station. She has no context about you,

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:13.880
what you want, who you are, and that's

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:16.502
why Gemini has gems to fix that. They

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:18.840
are your experts who remember who

00:03:16.502 --> 00:03:20.880
[snorts] they are and who you are. You

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:23.760
can build a gem that's your finance

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:26.840
advisor, a writing partner, or a health

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:29.120
coach. They remember and they're always

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:32.000
ready. And now the top floor is [music]

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:34.120
tools. This is where your execution

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.000
lives, your workspace. This is where

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:39.880
intelligence escapes the prompt window

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:42.560
and enters your actual work. Drafting

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:45.560
emails, building decks, summarizing

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:48.200
meetings, updating documents, and moving

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.720
the work forward. So those are the four

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:52.600
floors. Notebook LM grounds you in

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:55.480
evidence. Gemini [music] helps you

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:58.760
explore with clarity and massive

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:01.360
context. Gems give you that staff of

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:04.640
specialists, and workspace [music] turns

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:06.960
insights into tangible work. And just

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:09.840
understanding the blueprints of these

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.320
four floors already puts you ahead of

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:15.520
everyone else still digging holes in the

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:18.200
sand. Now, let's build it one floor at a

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:20.160
time. The biggest learning myth is that

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:22.880
mastery comes from consuming more

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:25.520
information. More books, more courses,

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:28.240
more content, but that's not how our

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:30.880
brain learns. Back in high school and

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.400
college, I constantly struggled with

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.103
learning and retention.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.360
I was not a very good student.

00:04:35.103 --> 00:04:37.280
>> [music]

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:40.160
>> Things changed later when I started

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:43.600
understanding how memory works. Working

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.560
memory is tiny. Try to shove a 500-page

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.800
textbook through it and you're trying to

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:50.120
squeeze an entire mountain through a

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:52.720
straw. Real learning happens when the

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:55.840
material gets moved into long-term

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:58.880
memory. Apps like notebook LM change the

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:01.480
speed and [music] shape of that process.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:04.120
Here's how. The brain moves information

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:07.000
into long-term memory through two modes,

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:09.840
focus mode and diffuse mode. So once you

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:12.600
load the material into notebook LM,

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:15.280
focus mode is where you actively

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:18.320
investigate it. Follow the breadcrumbs,

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:20.298
find the patterns. But the real aha

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:20.920
moment happens when you leave the desk.

00:05:20.298 --> 00:05:23.960
[music]

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:27.000
Your diffused mode. Notebook LM lets you

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:30.200
turn your research and your reports into

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:32.280
interactive podcasts or debates. You can

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:34.720
listen to it while you are taking a

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:36.840
walk, or on your commute, or when you're

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:39.760
in the kitchen. And you can even jump in

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:42.160
anytime you want and ask questions to

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:44.520
steer the podcast hosts, which are just

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:47.240
AI agents, in real time. [music] So you

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:49.160
can turn your dead zone into a learning

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:51.083
zone. What's the action item? When do

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.960
you use notebook LM? Three situations.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:54.120
[music]

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:56.480
When you're drowning in material, when

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:59.160
you want precision and close enough is

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:01.960
not good enough, and when you want

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:05.494
knowledge to move across formats. Audio,

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.680
video, a deck, flashcards, infographics.

00:06:05.494 --> 00:06:09.320
>> [music]

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:11.760
>> Notebook LM lets you learn in the format

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:14.240
your brain prefers. But once you have

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:16.520
that foundation, you need an engine

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:19.400
powerful enough to do something with it.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:22.400
For that, we have to move up to the next

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:26.240
floor. Gemini can hold a huge amount of

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:30.240
context in one session. PDFs, videos,

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:32.520
audio, images, diagrams, code, and data.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:34.200
All of that gives you three real

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:37.000
advantages. First, [music]

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:39.440
Gemini learns from your past chats. It

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:42.200
starts to understand your preferences,

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:45.440
your goals, your tone, the way you

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:47.920
think. Second, it can read and generate

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:51.520
content in many formats. Interactive

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:54.120
docs, audio, charts, images, video, even

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:56.640
music nowadays. And third, it can do

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:58.560
deep research inside the prompt.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:01.360
Understand the question, plan the

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:04.280
research, search the web, evaluate the

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:07.440
findings, and return a report with

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:10.640
citations. That's a powerful engine. But

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:13.320
raw capacity alone is not enough. If you

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:16.240
cannot steer it, all that power only

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:18.520
gets you lost faster. This is where AIM

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:21.600
comes in. This is one micro framework

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:23.960
that I've shared before. A is for actor.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:26.680
Don't just ask Gemini for an answer,

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:28.520
tell the model who it's acting as. So

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:31.640
you could say, Gemini, you're the

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:34.400
world's most sought-after resume editor

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:37.080
and business writer. I is for input.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:40.120
Give it the context it needs. Don't just

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:42.435
say, "Hey, fix my resume." Feed it your

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:44.640
resume, the job description, interview

00:07:42.435 --> 00:07:47.560
[music] notes, other resumes, company

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:50.000
research. M is for mission. You can be

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:53.120
precise about the outcome you want. Give

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:56.080
AI a clear mission. Like, "Give me five

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:58.720
specific ways to improve clarity and

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:01.480
impact of my resume and make sure I

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:04.520
increase my odds of getting an interview

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:07.440
at Nvidia for this product marketing

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:09.880
role." Now is time to build a team of

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:12.560
specialists. For that, let's move to the

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:15.200
next floor. Your staff is waiting for

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:17.520
you. The problem with AI is that it can

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:20.400
be very generic. That's why you need a

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:24.120
staff of specialists. And for that, you

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:26.560
create a gem. Give it a role, a tone, a

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:29.040
clear objective, and a knowledge base.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:31.280
And now it remembers everything. Not

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:34.400
just across one chat, but across the

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:36.840
entire arc of your work. If Gemini is

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:39.360
your general-purpose reasoning engine,

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:41.840
gems are your specialists that you can

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:44.440
build around your recurring themes. Like

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:46.920
a writing coach, a coding partner, a

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:49.160
research analyst, a brand consultant, a

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:53.720
chief of staff, a devil's advocate. Some

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:56.000
even build a BFF or a romantic partner.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:59.680
I haven't built that. You're changing

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:02.880
the game. Remember, gems are not folders

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:06.320
because folders organize information.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:08.880
Gems organize behavior. It's a much

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:12.240
bigger idea. A folder remembers where

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:15.000
your files are. A gem remembers who you

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:18.520
are, what you care about, and how you

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:21.080
think. And yes, you can feed any gem any

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:23.560
source material, including the notebooks

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:25.600
you built in notebook LM when you were

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:28.040
on the ground floor. Remember? And

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:31.800
suddenly, instead of organizing

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:33.920
documents, you're organizing expertise.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:36.680
Now you're building a staff of expert

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:39.240
agents who never start from zero and who

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:41.800
never go to sleep. The last problem is

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:43.960
fragmentation. Too many tools, too many

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:46.920
tabs, too many disconnected islands of

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:48.880
work. You need a single workhorse.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:51.360
Research suggests that when you are

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:54.000
context switching while working, it can

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:56.280
eat up as much as 40% of your

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:59.160
productivity time. We've all felt it,

00:09:56.280 --> 00:10:02.320
right? Our work is scattered across too

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:05.200
many places. We write in one place,

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:07.120
store it in second, analyze in third,

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:09.920
share it in fourth. There's no

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:12.720
connecting thread that hold it all

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:15.360
together. That's what makes Gemini

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:18.520
inside Google Workspace extremely

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:21.600
useful. Gemini is no longer a genie

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:25.520
trapped in chat window. Your Docs, your

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:28.080
Gmail, Drive, Calendar, Sheets, even the

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:31.000
meetings, they stop acting like isolated

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:34.200
islands and start behaving like one

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:36.520
single connected environment. And this

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:39.240
helps you relieve three big work

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:41.640
pressures: friction, focus, [music] and

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:43.640
flavor. First, friction. Imagine you're

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:46.200
applying for a job. Your story is

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:48.240
scattered everywhere: in your resume, in

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:51.000
your job description, old interview

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:54.000
notes, contact list, company research,

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:56.960
old recruiter emails. But now you can go

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:59.400
to Google Drive [music] and just ask AI,

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:01.839
"What are the biggest gaps in my fit?

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:03.880
What do I do next?" You're no longer

00:11:01.839 --> 00:11:06.920
stuck in a file cabinet. [music] You can

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:10.520
now refine and reconstruct your entire

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:12.720
story. Second, focus. Last week, I was

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:15.000
running late for a virtual meeting. We

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:17.320
were using Google Meet, and I joined it

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:20.000
5 minutes late. As soon as I joined,

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:22.520
Google Meet AI asked if I wanted to

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:24.760
catch up. I clicked yes, and it showed

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:26.600
me three bullet points of what I had

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:29.560
missed. I did not have to interrupt the

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:31.440
room and make everybody rewind.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:33.520
I thought it was brilliant. Everyone

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:36.920
stayed focused. [music] And third,

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:40.080
flavor. Now, this one matters way more

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:42.720
than we realize. Because AI can now

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:44.720
learn from the files in your Drive, it

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:48.000
can start to understand the entire

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:50.028
history of what you've generated. It can

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.640
see how you write and how you think.

00:11:50.028 --> 00:11:54.320
[music]

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:58.000
It's no longer about AI writing for you,

00:11:54.320 --> 00:12:00.960
it's about AI writing with you. So that

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:03.680
is your human intelligence system, an

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:06.640
architecture that you build with four

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:09.839
floors, four different jobs. But here's

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:13.360
why all of this actually matters at a

00:12:09.839 --> 00:12:15.520
deeper level. AI will eliminate some

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:19.080
jobs, for sure. [music] It will create

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:21.240
many new ones, and it'll reshape almost

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:24.400
all of them. Now, [music] I don't think

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:27.680
AI is replacing us, because every job

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:29.800
has two functions: mechanics [music]

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:32.080
and meaning. AI may change the

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:35.320
mechanics. It does not automatically

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:38.280
change or eliminate the meaning. That's

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:40.600
what humans are for. So this human

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:44.240
intelligence system that we talked about

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:47.480
here is not just about building your

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:50.080
edge. It's also about building [music]

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:52.600
yourself. You can use it to create

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:55.480
something real, something beautiful,

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:58.800
something constructive. Your worth is

00:12:55.480 --> 00:13:01.320
not a number that has to keep growing to

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:04.120
prove that you matter.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:06.009
You were born with it. To borrow from

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:06.280
Maya Angelou,

00:13:06.009 --> 00:13:08.000
>> [music]

